# Control flow

## Minimize `else`, `elseif`, and `else if`

Prefer **guard clauses** and **early return** so the happy path and each branch stay flat and named.

```php
// Avoid
if ($existing === null) {
    $this->create(...);
} elseif ($existing->value === $value) {
    $this->delete(...);
} else {
    $this->update(...);
}

// Prefer
if ($existing === null) {
    return $this->createVote(...);
}
if ($existing->value === $value) {
    return $this->removeVote($existing);
}
return $this->switchVote($existing, $value);
```

When branches differ in **both** persistence and result, extract **private methods** (one scenario per method) instead of growing a single `if/elseif/else` block.

## When a chain is acceptable

- Simple two-way branching with symmetric logic.
- `match` on a scalar/enum with exhaustive cases (no nested `else`).

## Do not

- Add `else` after `return` in the same block — it is dead noise.
- Use `elseif` to chain unrelated business scenarios — split into methods or a `match` on an explicit state enum.

**Reference:** `VoteService::toggle()`, `createVote()`, `removeVote()`, `switchVote()`.
